{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: complete G5 Membership8 invitation review at 8e8fffa23ad038aeb7ff140823fb69b7a3ae0d92, tree c40b02ae75fdcd06dbdde8f04a137b684f5afda8. No required findings.\n\nI read primary 66b0134c first in full, then inspected all nine exact changed-path Sources, the live builder promise cfcae5f0 and request 355b0266. Native prepare assigns all nine to this implementation. Each current Source is effective, fresh, not retired and not describing a superseded world. Old live predecessors and succession_unrecorded remain visible. Phase1 exposes no separate self_stale or structured authorization field; neither is inferred. Planner survey 61ace626 and future device-sign-in request abe69eeb were read. The future request adds no work to this candidate.\n\nThe shared client list covers exactly seven implemented person-invitation versions. Page admission, retained custody and CLI person join use it. Page and CLI additionally require a native membership join act. The configured service, complete references, handle and invitation-number checks remain. Membership8 uses the existing invitation-and-proof encoder; the private invitation seed is absent from the signed act. Web Locks remain required. The source diff changes only the nine declared paths from reviewed Main a9094eb1; all 2,612 other Main paths and modes are exact. No F1 graft is present.\n\nBoth closed grants were verified before their explicit leaves were read or copied. All 26,292 combined leaves were stable, physically copied and rehashed. Independent metadata checks matched all 2,621 gate snapshot blobs and modes to actual candidate Git objects. Every historical input-map row matches its snapshot. The pre-gate owning snapshot differs in generated assets and the native test's stand-in comment only; the exact-head gate and independent run cover the final bytes.\n\nOriginal evidence: twelve focused cases and seven compiler configurations pass. Native Membership6 and8 invitations complete the actual